    "text": "Analyze a script to identify character, setting and plot. Technical theatre is the appropriate selection, construction, and manipulation of those staging variables that visually and aurally support the performer and the needs of the production. Students will demonstrate the concepts, skills and attitudes of the technical theatre discipline through a different component at each level. Possible components of study include: lighting, sound, makeup, costume, set, properties, puppetry, mask, visual media, and management (stage/house/business). Advanced",
